## Database

{{#if (eq phpOrm "eloquent")}}
Eloquent stores notes in SQLite. {{#if (eq phpWebFramework "laravel")}}`app/Models/Note.php` is the model and `database/migrations/` owns the schema. Set DB_DATABASE to choose the file; it defaults to `database/database.sqlite`.{{else}}`src/Notes.php` boots the Illuminate Database Capsule, `src/Entity/Note.php` is the model, and `Notes::migrate` creates the table. Set DATABASE_PATH to choose the file; it defaults to `var/database.sqlite`.{{/if}}
{{else if (eq phpOrm "doctrine")}}
Doctrine ORM stores notes in SQLite. `src/Entity/Note.php` maps the entity with PHP attributes. {{#if (eq phpWebFramework "symfony")}}DoctrineBundle is configured in `src/Kernel.php` and `src/Controller/NotesController.php` uses the entity manager.{{else}}`src/Notes.php` creates the entity manager and uses Doctrine's schema tool.{{/if}} Set DATABASE_PATH to choose the file; it defaults to `var/database.sqlite`.
{{else if (eq phpOrm "cycle")}}
Cycle ORM stores notes in SQLite. `src/Notes.php` declares the ORM schema, creates the table through Cycle Database and persists `src/Entity/Note.php`. Set DATABASE_PATH to choose the file; it defaults to `var/database.sqlite`.
{{/if}}

Run `composer run db:setup` once before `composer run dev`. `GET /api/notes` lists notes. `POST /api/notes` accepts `{"title":"..."}` with 1 to 120 bytes of trimmed text and returns 201 with `id` and `title`. Invalid notes return 422 and malformed JSON returns 400. {{#if (eq phpTesting "none")}}`composer run proof:http` uses{{else}}`composer test` and `composer run proof:http` use{{/if}} temporary SQLite databases. Migrations beyond this starter schema are not generated.

{{/if}}
{{#if (ne phpAuth "none")}}
## Authentication

`GET /api/me` requires `Authorization: Bearer <token>` and returns `{"subject":"..."}` from the token's `sub` claim. Missing, malformed, expired or foreign tokens return 401 JSON with `WWW-Authenticate: Bearer`. Tokens must be HS256 JWTs signed with JWT_SECRET (at least 32 bytes) and carry `exp`, the JWT_ISSUER issuer and the JWT_AUDIENCE audience. Every token is rejected until JWT_SECRET is set.

{{#if (eq phpAuth "firebase-jwt")}}
`{{phpSourceDirectory}}/TokenVerifier.php` verifies tokens with firebase/php-jwt.
{{else if (eq phpAuth "lcobucci-jwt")}}
`{{phpSourceDirectory}}/TokenVerifier.php` verifies tokens with lcobucci/jwt signature, issuer, audience and time constraints.
{{else}}
Symfony Security protects `/api/me` with a stateless `access_token` firewall configured in `src/Kernel.php`. `src/Security/BearerTokenHandler.php` turns a verified token into a user, using `src/TokenVerifier.php` with firebase/php-jwt.
{{/if}}
This starter verifies tokens; it does not log users in. Issue tokens from your identity provider with the same secret, issuer and audience. For local testing, `composer run token:issue -- <subject>` prints a 15-minute token signed with JWT_SECRET.

{{/if}}
## Configuration and extension

{{#if (eq phpWebFramework "laravel")}}
Composer copies `.env.example` to `.env` after install when `.env` is missing. Laravel loads `.env` itself; `config/cors.php` reads CORS_ORIGIN and `bin/serve.php` reads HOST and PORT. Run `php artisan key:generate` before adding sessions, cookies or encryption. Exported environment variables take precedence. HOST defaults to 127.0.0.1 and PORT to 8080. Set CORS_ORIGIN to a comma-separated list of exact allowed origins. A composed web graph includes each frontend's development origin. Requests from other origins receive no CORS header.
{{else if (eq phpWebFramework "symfony")}}
Copy `.env.example` to `.env` if local configuration is needed. `Environment::load` reads only APP_ENV, APP_DEBUG, HOST, PORT and CORS_ORIGIN as INI strings. APP_ENV defaults to `prod`; the compiled container is cached in `var/cache/`. Exported environment variables take precedence. HOST defaults to 127.0.0.1 and PORT to 8080. Set CORS_ORIGIN to a comma-separated list of exact allowed origins. A composed web graph includes each frontend's development origin. Requests from other origins receive no CORS header.
{{else}}
Copy `.env.example` to `.env` if local configuration is needed. `Environment::load` reads only HOST, PORT and CORS_ORIGIN as INI strings. Exported environment variables take precedence. HOST defaults to 127.0.0.1 and PORT to 8080. Set CORS_ORIGIN to a comma-separated list of exact allowed origins. A composed web graph includes each frontend's development origin. Requests from other origins receive no CORS header.
{{/if}}

{{#if (eq phpWebFramework "laravel")}}
